package di

import (
	"__module__/internal/config"
	"__module__/internal/mailsender"
)

// NewMailSender is the optional SMTP sender provider the Loom graph binds, and
// this file is the stable integration seam for wiring mail into the Loom
// application.
//
// weld writes this file once, when both the mail and loom capabilities are
// installed, and never rewrites it while it regenerates the graph (di.go,
// loom_gen.go): edits below survive every later `weld add`.
//
// The sender is an available binding, not part of the default composition: the
// graph declares NewMailSender, but nothing depends on *mailsender.Sender, so
// Loom prunes it and an ordinary serve never constructs a sender and never needs
// a mail setting. To use mail, make a provider the graph already consumes depend
// on *mailsender.Sender. For an api+loom project, edit internal/di/api_provider.go
// (the API service seam) to take *mailsender.Sender; Loom then constructs
// NewMailSender and validates the mail configuration.
//
// Construction never sends and never connects: mailsender.New only validates the
// mail section and stores the settings, and the sender dials the SMTP server
// once per Send. There is no queue and no outbox, so this provider needs no
// lifecycle cleanup.
func NewMailSender(cfg *config.Config) (*mailsender.Sender, error) {
	return mailsender.New(cfg)
}
